Review fixes for opentracker 1c7fac4 (2026-09-06), seven findings from a source review, each
traced by a second reader and adversarially reviewed as a patch, then built and put through a lab
(announce, scrape, /stats, sixty SIGHUP reloads under load and valgrind). Apply from inside the
opentracker source directory with `patch -p1 --forward < opentracker-review-fixes.patch`, after
sighup-udp-workers.patch and udp-reject-interval.patch. None of these touches the per-packet or
per-announce path beyond one atomic add; none grows memory. The write-up for upstream is
UPSTREAM-REPORT.md.

  1. ot_udp.c: the UDP connection-id secret comes from getrandom(2), not srandom(time(NULL))
  2. ot_accesslist.c: a reload keeps the superseded list alive for the grace period whatever its age (use-after-free on SIGHUP)
  3. ot_http.c: a /stats task is cancelled when its client disconnects, like the fullscrape tasks (result delivered to a reused fd)
  4. ot_mutex.c: g_torrent_count is updated atomically instead of after the bucket lock is dropped
  5. ot_http.c: the tpbs stats path no longer writes one byte past a full request buffer
  6. opentracker.c: UDP worker threads start after trackerlogic_init and the first accesslist load, not during option parsing
  7. ot_accesslist.c: a whitelist whose last line has no newline no longer reads one byte past the mmap


